        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a posted hunting tract, after being notified not to enter, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...66,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} had hung no-hunting signs along a 55-acre wooded tract and mailed {D} a letter the prior fall. On {DATE}, a game camera showed {D} walking in at 6 a.m. with a bow and settling into a tree stand. A deputy found {D}'s truck at a gravel pull-off. {DL} says the sign had fallen and {D} believed the tract was part of a hunting club lease.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Game Camera", "{D} walks in with a bow and climbs a tree stand at 6 a.m."), E(.document, 2, "Notice Letter", "A letter to {D} from {V} telling {D.him} to stay off the tract, signed for by {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Club Lease", "{DL} says a hunting club told {D.him} the tract was theirs.")],
        role: "Wildlife officer",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role with wildlife enforcement?", "\"I am a wildlife officer. I check hunters in the field, respond to trespass complaints, and make sure hunting is done on land where it is permitted.\""), .direct("What did {V} report about the 55-acre tract?", "\"That {V} had posted no-hunting signs around the tract and had mailed {D} a letter the prior fall telling {D.him} to stay off. {V} asked for a patrol.\""), .direct("What did the game camera show on {DATE}?", "\"{D} walking in at about 6 a.m. with a bow, going to a tree, and climbing into a stand. It took several clear photos along the way.\""), .direct("Where did you find {D}'s truck?", "\"At a gravel pull-off on the road that borders the tract. It was parked about two hundred yards from the stand.\""), .direct("What did you find when you reached the stand?", "\"{D} sitting in it with a bow and a few arrows. I called up to {D}, and {D} came down and talked to me without any trouble.\""), .direct("What did the notice letter say?", "\"That {V} did not allow hunting on the tract and that {D} must stay off. It was signed for by {D} at the post office the prior fall.\""), .cross("A sign had fallen near the pull-off, hadn't it?", "\"Yes. One was down near the pull-off, lying in the leaves. That is the nearest sign to where {D} parked.\""), .cross("{D} did not run when you approached, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D} climbed down and spoke to me politely. {D} told me where {D.he} parked and what {D.he} thought.\""), .cross("A hunting club in the area had leases nearby, didn't it?", "\"Yes. There is a club with leased land next to the tract. I understand a map from the club may have been unclear.\""), .cross("Many hunters rely on maps from clubs, don't they?", "\"They do. Boundaries in wooded land are not always clear, and mistakes happen. I took that into account in my report.\""), .cross("Signs were posted about every hundred yards, correct?", "\"Mostly. There were a few gaps, and one was down. {V} did put up a good number, and I counted most of them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} hunted on land after a written warning.", "A hunter misled by a club and a fallen sign."),
        allocution: "\"I should have checked the map.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had the letter taped inside {D.his} glovebox.", "The hunting club sent {DL} a map that showed {V}'s tract inside its lease by mistake."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you walk onto {V}'s tract with a bow?", "\"Yes. I did. I thought it was land my club leased, and I climbed into a stand to hunt at first light.\""), .direct("Why did you believe it was part of the club's land?", "\"The club sent me a map that showed the tract inside its lease. I trusted the map, and I did not walk the boundary myself.\""), .direct("Did you see any no-hunting signs?", "\"I saw one lying on the ground near the road. I did not see any others when I walked in, and I assumed that it had fallen.\""), .direct("Did you receive {V}'s letter the prior fall?", "\"Yes. I signed for it. I put it in my glovebox and did not look at the tract it described again.\""), .direct("Why was the letter in your glovebox?", "\"I did not know what to do with it. I did not connect it with that tract until later. I should have read it carefully and checked the map.\""), .direct("What did you do when the officer called up to you?", "\"I climbed down and told the officer everything. I showed the officer the map, and I asked where the boundary was.\""), .cross("You got a letter from {V} telling you to stay off, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I signed for it, and I should have remembered it.\""), .cross("You kept that letter in your glovebox the whole time, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not look at it. I know how it looks that I did not remember it.\""), .cross("You did not walk the boundary before you hunted, did you?", "\"No. I trusted the club's map. I should have checked the boundary myself.\""), .cross("You saw a fallen sign and walked in anyway, didn't you?", "\"I saw one on the ground. I did not stop to ask why it was there, and I should have.\""), .cross("You climbed into a tree stand on someone else's land, didn't you?", "\"I did. I did not know it was someone else's land. I know that does not excuse it.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} posted no-hunting signs around a 55-acre tract and mailed {D} a letter telling {D.him} to stay off. A game camera showed {D} walking in with a bow and climbing into a tree stand.", "{D} was misled by a hunting club's map and a fallen sign. {D} cooperated fully, and an honest mistake about a boundary is not a crime."),
        closings: ("A written warning, a signed receipt, a game camera, and a truck at the pull-off. {D} had been told to stay off the land and walked onto it anyway.", "The club's map showed the tract in its lease, and one sign had fallen. {D} did not run or hide, and told the officer exactly what happened."),
        timeline: [(-300, "{V} mails the warning letter."), (0, "6 a.m.: {DL} enters the tract."), (0, "7:15 a.m.: {V} reviews the game camera."), (0, "8 a.m.: a wildlife officer arrives.")],
        identified: "{V}'s game camera and a truck at the pull-off.",
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .male])

    static let skateparkScuffleV1 = SmallCases.make(
