        summary: "{V}'s SUV was found on jack stands in the carport on {DATE}, its wheels gone. Ten days later, {V} spotted rims with a distinctive chip on a utility trailer parked at {D}'s home. A deputy confirmed the serial marks. {DL} says {D.he} took them in trade for a day's welding.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Rims and Tires", "Four rims with {V}'s etched mark and a chipped lip, on {D}'s trailer.", .search), E(.document, 2, "Purchase Invoice", "{V}'s invoice listing the rim model and serial marks.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Trade for Welding", "{DL} says a stranger traded the set for a weld job.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What was reported stolen from {V}'s carport on {DATE}?", "\"The wheels from an SUV that was left on jack stands. All four wheels and tires were taken in the night, and the vehicle was found sitting on the stands.\""), .direct("How did {V} come across the wheels again?", "\"Ten days later, {V} spotted rims with a distinctive chip on a utility trailer parked at {D}'s home. {V} called us right away.\""), .direct("What did you do when you got there?", "\"I went to the trailer and checked the rims. I read the serial marks and compared them with {V}'s purchase invoice. They matched.\""), .direct("Where exactly were the wheels at {D}'s home?", "\"On a trailer by {D}'s carport, in the open, where anyone could see them from the road. Nothing was covered or hidden.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you about how they got there?", "\"That a stranger traded the set for a weld job. {D} said {D.he} did a day of welding and was handed the wheels as payment.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the person {D} named?", "\"Only a first name. We later learned that a tradesman who offered such sets pleaded guilty to other wheel thefts and named {D} as a buyer.\""), .cross("The wheels were in plain view, weren't they?", "\"Yes. They were on a trailer next to the carport. {D} did not hide them or move them when we arrived.\""), .cross("{D} gave you a first name, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A first name only. It was a consistent story, and {D} did not change it.\""), .cross("The tradesman later told investigators {D} did not know the wheels were stolen, didn't that person?", "\"Yes. The tradesman said {D} did not know. I am aware of that, and it is part of the record.\""), .cross("You did not see {D} take the wheels from the carport, did you?", "\"No. No one did. The wheels were taken in the night, and no witness saw it.\""), .cross("A day of welding is real work, isn't it?", "\"It is, and {D} does weld for a living. I have no reason to doubt that {D} did the job.\"")],
