        role: "Sheriff's detective",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at {V}'s home at about 12:40 a.m. on {DATE}?", "\"Three shots came through {V}'s bedroom window. One fragment cut {V}'s arm. {V} was awake and dove to the floor, and then called 911.\""), .direct("What did {V}'s doorbell camera capture?", "\"A dark sedan stopping in front of the house and a flash from the passenger window. The plate was not visible, and the faces were not clear.\""), .direct("How did {D} become a suspect?", "\"{V} named {D}, a former partner who had left angry voicemails for a month. The messages threatened {V} and used {V}'s name directly.\""), .direct("What was found behind {D}'s property?", "\"A revolver in a creek, with a spent round still in the cylinder. A deputy recovered it, and ballistics compared it with the fragments.\""), .direct("What did you find on {D}'s car?", "\"Gunshot residue on the passenger door handle. That is consistent with someone firing from the passenger window and touching the handle.\""), .direct("What did {D} say about the revolver?", "\"That {D} sold it months earlier. {D} produced a receipt dated before the shooting that bears a buyer's signature.\""), .cross("The plate on the sedan was not visible, was it?", "\"No. I cannot say from the camera that the car was {D}'s. It was a dark sedan, similar to {D}'s, but not matched.\""), .cross("A neighbor says {D}'s car was in the driveway at 12:30, doesn't the neighbor?", "\"Yes. That is in my file. It is a statement that cuts the other way, and I considered it.\""), .cross("The receipt for the revolver is dated before the shooting, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It is dated months before. I could not locate the buyer, and I cannot say the sale did not happen.\""), .cross("Many dark sedans are on the road, aren't there?", "\"Yes. It is a very common type of car. I do not rely on the model alone.\""), .cross("You do not know who held the revolver on the night of the shooting, do you?", "\"No. I know where it was found. I do not know who held it that night.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's neighbor",
