        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Empty Rifle", "{DL} says the rifle was empty.")],
        role: "Teen witness",
        exam: [.direct("Where were you and your friends going on {DATE}?", "\"To a pond on the other side of an orchard. We took a shortcut through the trees because it saved about ten minutes, and the day was hot.\""), .direct("What happened when you got near the packing shed?", "\"{D} came around the corner with a rifle and pointed it right at us. {D} yelled at us to freeze or we would get shot.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I pulled out my phone and filmed. I was scared and my hands were shaking, but I wanted proof. My friends froze with their hands in the air.\""), .direct("How did the rifle look when it was pointed at you?", "\"Long, dark and steady. I could see right down the barrel. It was aimed at one of us for several seconds, and then it swept across all three.\""), .direct("What did {D} say after you stopped?", "\"{D} yelled that we were trespassing and stealing. {D} told us to get out and never come back, and we ran toward the road.\""), .direct("What did you do after you got away?", "\"We called our parents and then the sheriff's office. I showed the deputy the video, and my friends gave statements.\""), .cross("One of you grabbed an apple, didn't you?", "\"One of us picked one up from the ground. We did not take anything else, and we did not know it was a problem.\""), .cross("You did not see a no-trespassing sign until later, did you?", "\"Not until afterward. We came in from a side path and did not walk by the main sign.\""), .cross("You were on {D}'s land, weren't you?", "\"I think so. We cut through the orchard. We did not know whose land it was exactly.\""), .cross("You did not see whether the rifle was loaded, did you?", "\"No. I could not tell. All I knew was that it was pointed at me, and I was terrified.\""), .cross("{D} did not fire the rifle, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D} never fired it. But I did not know whether {D} would, and that is what scared me.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} aimed a rifle at three teens.", "A warning with an empty rifle."),
        allocution: "\"I was wrong to aim at kids.\"",
        truths: ("A deputy found a round in the chamber at the scene.", "A neighbor says teens had been stripping the orchard for weeks."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you point a rifle at the three teens?", "\"Yes. I did. I raised it to scare them off, and I regret it. I should never have aimed it at anyone.\""), .direct("Why did you aim it?", "\"They were walking through my orchard, and I had been losing fruit for weeks. I got angry and reached for the rifle without thinking.\""), .direct("Was the rifle loaded?", "\"I thought it was empty. I did not check the chamber, and I learned later that a round was in it.\""), .direct("What had been happening in the orchard?", "\"For weeks someone had been stripping trees and leaving a mess. I posted a sign and I watched the rows, and nothing changed.\""), .direct("What did you do after the teens ran?", "\"I put the rifle down and called the sheriff's office myself. I told them what I had done and where to find me.\""), .direct("What would you say to the teens?", "\"That I am sorry. I scared you badly, and no fruit is worth that. I should have called the sheriff's office instead.\""), .cross("A round was in the chamber when the deputy checked, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not know. I should have checked before I ever picked it up.\""), .cross("You yelled that they would get shot, didn't you?", "\"I yelled to freeze. I may have said more. I know what I said was frightening.\""), .cross("You aimed a rifle at three teens over some fruit, didn't you?", "\"I did. It was a terrible choice, and I would give anything to take it back.\""), .cross("You could have called the sheriff's office first, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I could have. I did not, and I know that is what I should have done.\""), .cross("You pointed a rifle at a person who was holding a phone, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not see the phone until later. I just saw three people in my orchard.\"")],
        openings: ("Three teens took a shortcut through an orchard on the way to a pond. {D} came around a packing shed and leveled a rifle at them, and one teen filmed it.", "{D} had been losing fruit for weeks and meant only to scare off trespassers. {D} believed the rifle was empty and called the sheriff afterward."),
        closings: ("The video shows {D} aiming a rifle at three teens and yelling that they would be shot. A deputy found a round in the chamber.", "Trespassers had stripped the orchard for weeks, a sign was posted, and {D} believed the rifle was empty. It was a warning born of frustration."),
        timeline: [(0, "3:30 p.m.: the teens cross the orchard."), (0, "3:35 p.m.: {DL} aims the rifle."), (0, "4 p.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "A teen's phone video.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a firearm"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["selfDefense"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .male])

    static let dumpsterFireV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.dumpsterFire",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Grocery Loading Dock Dumpster Torched Before Dawn", "Fired Stock Clerk Questioned After Blaze"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a commercial dumpster, by fire, causing damage of $850, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A dumpster at the back of {V}'s grocery store burned at 4:40 a.m. on {DATE} and the fire was put out before it reached the wall. Two days earlier {V} had let {D} go for repeated lateness. A dock camera showed someone in a rain poncho lighting a bundle of cardboard. {DL} says {D.he} was asleep and that ponchos are sold in every store.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Dock Camera", "A poncho-clad figure lights cardboard and tosses it into the dumpster."), E(.document, 2, "Fire Marshal's Report", "Cardboard ignited by an open flame; no accelerant.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Asleep", "{DL}'s sister says {D.he} was asleep at her apartment.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find when you investigated the dumpster fire on {DATE}?", "\"A burned dumpster at the back of the grocery store. The fire started at 4:40 a.m. and was put out before it reached the wall of the building.\""), .direct("How was the fire started?", "\"Cardboard was ignited by an open flame. We found no accelerant in the debris, and the pattern was consistent with a lit bundle tossed into the container.\""), .direct("What did the dock camera show?", "\"A figure in a rain poncho lighting a bundle of cardboard with a flame and tossing it into the dumpster. The hood hid the face.\""), .direct("What was found in {D}'s car?", "\"A rain poncho in the trunk with scorch marks on the sleeve. It was similar to the one on camera, though it is a common type.\""), .direct("What did you learn about {D}'s connection to the store?", "\"The owner had let {D} go for repeated lateness two days before. {D} was a former employee who knew the back dock.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the time on the camera?", "\"The camera clock was an hour fast. We checked it against the fire dispatch times, and that is how we reconciled them.\""), .cross("The face on the video is hidden, isn't it?", "\"Yes. The poncho hood covers the face. I cannot say who is in the video from the image alone.\""), .cross("Ponchos are sold at every store, aren't they?", "\"Yes. They are cheap and very common. I would not rely on the poncho alone.\""), .cross("The lighter found on {D} was a common brand, wasn't it?", "\"It was a common disposable lighter. Thousands of people carry the same kind.\""), .cross("The fire did not spread to the building, did it?", "\"No. It was put out before it reached the wall. The damage was limited to the dumpster.\""), .cross("You do not know where {D} was at 4:40 a.m., do you?", "\"I know what {D} says and what a relative says. I cannot confirm it either way from my own investigation.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned the dumpster after being let go.", "A poncho on video and a sleeping alibi."),
        allocution: "\"I was mad about my job.\"",
        truths: ("A poncho with scorch marks was in {DL}'s trunk.", "{DL}'s sister admits {D.he} was asleep on her couch when the video was taken, but the camera clock was an hour fast."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you set the dumpster on fire?", "\"No. I did not. I was asleep at my relative's apartment when that fire started, and I did not leave the couch all night.\""), .direct("Why were you let go from the grocery store?", "\"For being late too many times. I had a long commute and a sick family member, and I could not make it on time. It hurt.\""), .direct("How did you feel about being let go?", "\"Angry and embarrassed. I felt like I was treated unfairly, but I never planned to hurt anyone or the store.\""), .direct("Why do you own a poncho?", "\"For work and for the rain. I keep one in my trunk. It is scorched because I used it near a grill, and it has nothing to do with this.\""), .direct("Where were you at 4:40 that morning?", "\"At my relative's place, on the couch. I fell asleep watching TV, and my relative can say I was there.\""), .direct("What did you do when you learned about the fire?", "\"I was shocked. I told the deputies where I had been and offered to let them check my phone and my car.\""), .cross("You were angry at {V}, weren't you?", "\"A little, yes. I was upset about losing my job. That does not mean I would burn a dumpster.\""), .cross("A poncho with scorch marks was in your trunk, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was scorched at a grill earlier. I understand how it looks.\""), .cross("Your relative is the one who says you were asleep, isn't it?", "\"Yes. My relative was there. No one else can say, because we were the only two in the apartment.\""), .cross("You knew the back dock of the store well, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I worked there for two years. That is also why I would not have lit a fire there.\""), .cross("The camera clock was an hour fast, wasn't it?", "\"The investigators say so. It makes it harder to say when the fire was lit, and I cannot explain that.\"")],
        openings: ("A dumpster at the back of a grocery store burned at 4:40 a.m., two days after {D} was let go. A dock camera showed a figure in a rain poncho lighting cardboard, and a scorched poncho was in {D}'s trunk.", "{D} was asleep at a relative's home. A poncho on video is something thousands of people own, and the camera clock was wrong."),
        closings: ("A poncho-clad figure on the dock camera, a scorched poncho in {D}'s trunk, and a motive from a firing two days earlier. The evidence points to {D}.", "The figure on the video has no face, ponchos are sold in every store, and the camera clock was off by an hour. {D} was asleep."),
        timeline: [(-2, "{V} lets {DL} go."), (0, "4:40 a.m.: the dumpster is lit."), (0, "4:50 a.m.: firefighters put it out."), (1, "A deputy interviews {DL}.")],
        identified: "{V}'s suspicion and a dock camera.",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let parkingKnifeIntentV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.parkingKnifeIntent",
