        allocution: "\"I lost my cool again.\"",
        truths: ("The alley's lane camera shows {DL} take the first swing.", "{V}'s bag stayed on {V.his} shoulder until after the punch."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you punch {V}?", "\"Yes. I did. I punched {V} in the face, and I wish I had not. I have regretted it every day since.\""), .direct("Why did you punch {V}?", "\"I thought {V} was about to swing a ball bag at me. I saw the strap go up, and I reacted before I could think.\""), .direct("What was the argument about?", "\"A foul line call. I thought the call was wrong, and we both got loud. It got personal faster than I expected.\""), .direct("Did the bag hit you?", "\"No. It never touched me. I hit first, and I realized afterward that it had not been swung.\""), .direct("What do you remember about your earlier convictions?", "\"I was younger and angrier then. I took a class and tried to change, and I felt like I had. I am sorry I let it happen again.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"That I am sorry. You did not deserve to be hit over a bowling call, and I will pay for any medical bills.\""), .cross("The lane camera shows you taking the first swing, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I know. I swung first, and I understand the bag was on {V}'s shoulder.\""), .cross("You have two earlier assault convictions, don't you?", "\"Yes. Two. I know how it looks to have a third.\""), .cross("The bag never left {V}'s shoulder before you swung, did it?", "\"The video says it stayed. I thought I saw it move. I may have been wrong.\""), .cross("You could have walked away from the argument, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have. I let my temper get ahead of me again.\""), .cross("{V} did not hit you, did {V}?", "\"No. {V} did not touch me. I know that now.\"")],
        openings: ("After a bowling league match, {D} and {V} argued over a foul line call. {D} punched {V} in the face, and {V}'s nose bled. {D} has two earlier assault convictions.", "{D} saw a ball bag lift and reacted in an instant. It was a bad reaction in a tense moment, not a plan to hurt anyone."),
        closings: ("A punch to the face, a bag still on {V}'s shoulder, and two earlier assault convictions. The lane camera shows {D} swung first.", "{V} lifted a bag in anger, and {D} reacted. A swing in a moment of fear is not the same as an attack."),
