        openings: ("{V} collapsed in a faculty lounge after drinking from a thermos. A lab found antifreeze in the thermos and in {V}'s blood, and a camera showed {D} entering with a small bottle at 7:20 a.m.", "{D} carried a bottle of hand sanitizer into the lounge. A hallway camera with a bad clock and an angry email are not proof of poison."),
        closings: ("Antifreeze in the thermos and in {V}'s blood, {D} on camera with a bottle, an angry email, and a jug of antifreeze with a scraped label in {D}'s garage.", "The bottle was sanitizer, four other people entered the lounge, and the camera clock was wrong. {D} had no reason to hurt anyone."),
