        truths: ("{DL}'s tow strap was stained with hedge sap and rust from the posts.", "{V} refused to read the survey for a year, a neighbor says."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you pull the fence out?", "\"Yes. I did, with a tow strap and a truck. I was angry and I thought I was within my rights.\""), .direct("Why did you pull it out?", "\"The fence was on my land. I warned {V} in writing, and {V} did not respond. I felt I had no other choice.\""), .direct("How did you know it was on your land?", "\"A survey showed it a foot over the line. I showed it to {V}, but {V} would not read it.\""), .direct("What did you do before you pulled it out?", "\"I sent a letter and called twice. I waited about a year, and nothing happened.\""), .direct("What did you do with the posts and the shrubs?", "\"I stacked them neatly at the edge of {V}'s yard. I did not throw them away. I wanted {V} to be able to put them back.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"That I am sorry for how I did it. I should have gone to court and not used a truck.\""), .cross("You did not wait for a court, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I should have, and I understand that.\""), .cross("You destroyed three posts, mesh and a hedge, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I damaged them. I will pay for what I destroyed.\""), .cross("You tied a strap to your truck and drove, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I lost my temper.\""), .cross("{V} refused to read the survey for a year, didn't {V}?", "\"That is what a neighbor says. I do not know about a year, but {V} never responded.\""), .cross("A boundary dispute belongs in civil court, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I know that now. I should have filed there.\"")],
